  "summary": "I am an electrical engineer from UT Dallas with a Bachelor's in Electrical Engineering and focus in microelectronics working in the high-tech Engineering field. As an award-winning inventor, I have learned to be creative and persistent when faced with challenges. Electrical engineering is not just a career path for me, it is also a lifelong hobby; my home contains a workshop that allows me to bring my concepts into fruition. \n\nCommunication Skills\nOver a period of 6 years, my communication skills have evolved. The evolution of my communication skills has shown itself over a period of 6 years. Speech courses, professional and technical communication classes, and capstone group presentations have fueled my success. I am comfortable presenting in front of peers, professors, and industry professionals. \n\nInterpersonal Skills\nMy project experience has included working in multicultural groups where my group problem solving, leadership, and technical skills have been broadened.\n\nInterests\nMy travel has included 14 countries, most recently walking from France 1200 km across Spain to the coast, taking me to places where I can experience diverse cultures and interactions, preparing me for a workplace where multiculturalism has become the norm. My other interests include performing and composing music for various instruments as well as playing soccer.",
