  "projects": [
   {
    "title": "SignalMe",
    "description": "This project is an augmented reality visualization of signal strengths within an Android application. A user can open the app and walk around the real work as spherical objects are dropped in the location of the phone in 3D space. These spheres are equipped with colors representing the signal strength at that position. The user is able to freely look around an area and perfectly visualize the strength of their phone signal via those spheres that have been dropping as they move around. GPS data is also collected along with signal data and logged for future applications that include mass data collection for 2D and 3D mapping of a carrier’s signal across a large area as well as for diagnostic and technical support structures.",
    "dateRange": {},
    "associatedWith": "Oct 2019 - Present"
   },
   {
    "title": "Cloud Hosted Intelligent Sprinkler System",
    "description": "An autonomous sprinkler system capable of monitoring outdoor conditions and adjusting sprinkler settings accordingly. The system will measure soil humidity, weather data, and watering schedules to determine which sprinklers in our network should run. Using local network connections, CC1310 Launchpads with WiFi Booster Packs, and Amazon Web Services, we will communicate moisture and weather data and switch sprinklers on and off. ​\n\nThe system will run underground and will be able to remain running with little to no physical maintenance. Devices running outside will be solar powered and switch on to transmit information periodically and minimize power usage.​\n\nUsing a cloud hosted web interface, a user will be able to input desired watering options and view live data of their outdoor conditions. The web interface will also allow the user to schedule watering and override computer settings. The current system status will also be provided.\n\n\nCurrent Project Status:\nAll hardware components have been assembled and tested - final housings and large-scale testing is still needed. The software team is working on a graphical user interface that is stored with user profiles on a web server. The networking team is in the process of ensuring precise and accurate timing of wireless communication between all outdoor sensors and the main hub.",
    "dateRange": {},
    "associatedWith": "Sep 2018 - Jul 2019"
   }
